8d77","position":{"commit_sha":"3568d2dbf15cfedcfdeedb982704e59824631fdd","position":"1785729767901015001-8a1e9487-abc7-4c94-bbb2-ac261b708d77"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"f9c694084a2ff85ef22156006fcd6f2fe7c339aa3990fc83087f08c046a73cef","event_uuid":"d5e41406-c237-485d-8f41-2e67542c2cf8","position":{"commit_sha":"075dc013ee3d487f39591457720abc73676d3556","position":"1785731366639912001-d5e41406-c237-485d-8f41-2e67542c2cf8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation landed for review: Gerrit change 1285 (commit 72f1a97f18, stacked on f1eb's 1275). TDD trail: oracle tests/unit/metrics/test_bug_trends.py (6 tests, happy-path contract incl. MISSING labeled cohort, clock seam, descending fan-in, registry ids/labels) + held-out test_bug_trends_heldout.py (15 tests: zero-bug/missing-tracker unavailability, non-bug exclusion, detected_by sibling-degradation independence, all-MISSING month, flow-vs-stock range semantics, single-sample percentiles, in_progress counts as open, unresolved caused_by target counted, UNLINK removal, registry evaluate Unavailable/MetricValue labels, CLI end-to-end fault-isolation rendering). RED confirmed (ModuleNotFoundError) before implementation. Subagent implemented to oracle only; orchestrator refactored (extracted pure _derive_* over rows, wired real ctx.analysis_cache sharing — subagent's cache path was dead code — hoisted datetime import). Held-out first exposure: 21/21 green. Mutation checks: 5/5 killed (drop-MISSING, ignore-range, floor-rank percentile, closed-leak open-age, ascending fan-in). tests/unit/metrics 109 passed; lint+mypy clean. Real-store smoke: close_class months incl. MISSING cohort for pre-convention July, ttc count=228, open age count=32, detected_by honestly unavailable (no bug carries d3ed field yet), fan-in descending. Awaiting LLM-Review + Verified on 1285.","timestamp":1785731366639912001}],"created_at":1785639977306473001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"24b213ef-256c-48a3-954a-7d761a67773f","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"d3ed-88e3-86a3-4918"},{"link_uuid":"6a41d254-b6dc-452c-b7b6-10a8326ff43a","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"c967-fc7c-8e4d-4b28"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n344 closed bugs exist but no lens aggregates them: close_class distribution over time, detection channel, open-bug age, caused_by fan-in (which components spawn bugs), time-to-close. Trend questions are answered today by ad-hoc scripts.\n\n## Approach\nAdd a bug_trends lens to the rebar metrics registry (same _spec() registration pattern as gate-economics sidecar metrics). Dimensions: close_class distribution bucketed by close month; detected_by distribution (populated as the detected-by sibling lands — lens must degrade gracefully while the field is sparse); open-bug age percentiles; caused_by link fan-in per target; time-to-close percentiles. Surface taxonomy-window skew INSIDE the computed value payload: the close_class distribution carries an explicit labeled MISSING bucket (the pre-convention era where close_class is absent for ~214 bugs) alongside the vocabulary classes, so eras are never silently mixed. (The registry source/confidence labels are closed spec-level vocabularies and cannot express per-cohort annotations; each spec registers as source=structural, confidence=high.)\n\nRange semantics (stock vs flow): the FLOW dimensions — close_class-by-month and time-to-close — filter on the close TRANSITION timestamp within the ctx since/until range, exactly as sibling event/sidecar metrics filter on their ranges; with the CLI default 30-day window the historical cohorts only appear when the caller widens --since (documented in the user-guide section). The STOCK dimensions — open-bug age percentiles, detected_by distribution, caused_by fan-in — are point-in-time measures over the current store and deliberately ignore the range (an age percentile or fan-in count has no flow window); this deviation from range-filtering siblings is stated here and in the module docstring.\n\n## Scope\n- src/rebar/metrics/bug_trends.py (new lens module; register() appends specs idempotently on id)\n- src/rebar/metrics/__init__.py (side-effect import of the new module alongside event_metrics/git_metrics/sidecar_metrics — without it REGISTRY never sees the lens)\n- docs/user-guide.md metrics section\n\n## Testing\nHappy path: synthetic store with classed+unclassed bugs -> lens returns distributions with era-skew labels. Edge: zero bugs -> 'unavailable' state per registry convention, not a crash or empty-implies-healthy. detected_by absent everywhere -> dimension reports unavailable, other dimensions unaffected.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] 'rebar metrics' exposes a bug_trends lens with the five dimensions, registered via the standard registry pattern.\n- [ ] Pre-convention MISSING close_class is surfaced as a labeled cohort, never silently dropped or merged.\n- [ ] Sparse/absent detected_by degrades that dimension to unavailable without affecting others.\n- [ ] Unit tests cover populated, empty, and mixed-era stores.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/metrics/registry.py","reason":"register bug_trends lens"},{"path":"src/rebar/metrics/event_metrics.py","reason":"bug event aggregations"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/metrics.py","reason":"CLI lens surface"},{"path":"docs/user-guide.md","reason":"lens docs"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["depends_on","d3ed-88e3-86a3-4918"],["parent","2f4c-7e5c-e782-4e97"],["relates_to","c967-fc7c-8e4d-4b28"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"2f4c-7e5c-e782-4e97","parent_status_uuid":"727053bf-4f7e-4dfa-8ed8-fa533ff047cf","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["bug-trends","metrics"],"ticket_id":"b967-8a1a-9bbb-4b86","ticket_type":"task","title":"bug_trends metrics lens (close-class, detected-by, age, caused_by fan-in, time-to-close)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["a2b4a63f-f479-4732-8466-3e3862056543","24b213ef-256c-48a3-954a-7d761a67773f","3cdea6de-e922-492a-86e4-49d88f183dc5","291d922f-36d2-4199-8a78-9e80eba134b2","c8fc4ecd-353f-4049-a9a1-fe36129eab99","34d560df-145f-4643-b5aa-9fdf85f7d29a","727053bf-4f7e-4dfa-8ed8-fa533ff047cf","8a1e9487-abc7-4c94-bbb2-ac261b708d77","d5e41406-c237-485d-8f41-2e67542c2cf8","6a41d254-b6dc-452c-b7b6-10a8326ff43a"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785738684772990401,"uuid":"94110b21-da50-4fd5-9bb2-9a9805a9989f"}